[2025-04-14 22:05:18,055][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,055][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "[0x9][0x9][0x9][0x9][0x9]<description><![CDATA[A Minnesota cybersecurity and computer forensics expert whose testimony has featured in thousands of courtroom trials over the past 30 years is facing questions about his credentials and an inquiry from the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI). Legal experts say the inquiry could be grounds to reopen a number of adjudicated cases in which the expert's testimony may have been pivotal.]]></description>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,055][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "[0x9][0x9][0x9][0x9][0x9][0x9][0x9][0x9][0x9][0x9]<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>A Minnesota cybersecurity and computer forensics expert whose testimony has featured in thousands of courtroom trials over the past 30 years is facing questions about his credentials and an inquiry from the <strong>Federal Bureau of Investigation</strong> (FBI). Legal experts say the inquiry could be grounds to reopen a number of adjudicated cases in which the expert&#8217;s testimony may have been pivotal.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,055][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<div id="attachment_70889" style="width: 827px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img aria-descr"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,055][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "ibedby="caption-attachment-70889" decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="size-full wp-image-70889" src="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/marklanterman-linkedin.png" alt="" width="817" height="597" srcset="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/marklanterman-linkedin.png 817w, https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/marklanterman-linkedin-768x561.png 768w, https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/marklanterman-linkedin-782x571.png 782w" sizes="(max-width: 817px) 100vw, 817px" /><p id="caption-attachment-70889" class="wp-caption-text">One might conclude from reading Mr. Lanterman&#8217;s LinkedIn profile that has a degree from Harvard University.</p></div>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,055][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p><strong><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/marklanterman" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mark Lanterman</a></strong> is a former investigator for the U.S. Secret Service Electronics Crimes Task Force who founded the Minneapolis consulting firm <strong>Computer Forensic Services</strong> (CFS). The CFS website says Lanterman&#8217;s 30-year career has seen him testify as an expert in more than 2,000 cases, with experience in cases involving sexual harassment and workplace claims, theft of intellectual property and trade secrets, white-collar crime, and class action lawsuits.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,055][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Or at least it did until last month, when Lanterman&#82"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,055][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "17;s profile and work history were quietly removed from the CFS website. The removal came after <strong>Hennepin County Attorney&#8217;s Office</strong> <a href="https://www.hennepinattorney.org/news/news/2025"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,131][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "/March/lanterman-disclosure" target="_blank" rel="noopener">said</a> it was notifying parties to ten pending cases that they were unable to verify Lanterman&#8217;s educational and employment background. The county attorney also said the FBI is now investigating the allegations.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,131][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Those allegations were raised by <strong>Sean Harrington</strong>, an attorn[\r][\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,131][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "8000[\r][\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,131][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "ey and forensics examiner based in Prescott, Wisconsin. Harrington alleged that Lanterman lied under oath in court on multiple occasions when he testified that he has a Bachelor of Science and a Master&#8217;s degree in computer science from the now-defunct <strong>Upsala College</strong>, and that he completed his postgraduate work in cybersecurity at <strong>Harvard University</strong>.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,131][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Harrington&#8217;s claims gained steam thanks to digging by the law firm <strong>Perkins Coie LLP</strong>, which is defending a case wherein a client&#8217;s laptop was forensically reviewed by Lanterman. On March 14, Perkins Coie attorneys <a href="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/155-1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">asked the judge</a> (PDF) to strike Lanterman&#8217;s testimony because neither he nor they could substantiate claims about his educational background.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,131][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Upsala College, located in East Orange, N.J., operated for 102 years until it closed in 1995 after a "
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "period of declining enrollment and financial difficulties. Perkins Coie told the court that they&#8217;d visited <strong>Felician University</strong>, which holds the transcripts for Upsala College during the years Lanterman claimed to have earned undergraduate and graduate degrees. The law firm said Felician <a href="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/155-21.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">had no record of transcripts for Lanterman</a> (PDF), and that his name was absent from all of the Upsala College student yearbooks and commencement programs during that period.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Reached for comment, Lanterman acknowledged he had no way to prove he attended Upsala College, and that his &#8220;postgraduate work&#8221; at Harvard was in fact an eight-week online cybersecurity class called <strong>HarvardX</strong>, which cautions that its certificates should not be considered equivalent to a Harvard degree or a certificate earned through traditional, in-person programs at Harvard University.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Lanterman has testified that his first job after college was serving as a police officer in Springfield Township, Pennsylvania, although the Perkins Coie attorneys noted that this role was omitted from his resume. The attorneys said when they tried to verify Lanterman&#8217;s work history, &#8220;the police department responded with a story that wo"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "uld be almost impossible to believe if it was not corroborated by Lanterman&#8217;s own email communications.&#8221;</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>As recounted in the March 14 filing, Lanterman was deposed on Feb. 11, and the following day <a href="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/155-21.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">he emailed the Springfield Township Police Department</a> to see if he could have a peek at his old personnel file. On Feb. 14, Lanterman visited the Springfield Township PD and asked to borrow his employment record. He told the officer he spoke with on the phone that he&#8217;d recently been instructed to &#8220;get his affairs in order&#8221; after being diagnosed with a grave heart condition, and that he wanted his old file to show his family about his early career.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>According to Perkins Coie, Lanterman left the Springfield Township PD with his personnel file, and has not returned it as promised.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>&#8220;It is shocking that an expert from Minnesota would travel to suburban Philadelphia and abscond with his decades-old personnel file to obscure his background,&#8221; the law firm wrote. &#8220;That appears to be the worst and most egregious form of spoliation, and the deception alone is reason enough to exclude Lanterman and consider sanctions.&#8221;</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Harrington initially contacted KrebsOnSecurity about his concerns i"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "n late 2023, fuming after sitting through <a href="https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/srxrxkwyf03inudrw9ymn/2023-Seminar-Recording-copy-copy-1.MP4?rlkey=th0yqylm5uvmq84skfg8qvfh3&amp;e=1&amp;dl=0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">a conference speech</a> in which Lanterman shared documents from a ransomware victim and told attendees it was because they&#8217;d refused to hire his company to perform a forensic investigation on a recent breach.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>&#8220;He claims he was involved in the Martha Stewart investigation, the Bernie Madoff trial, Paul McCartney[0xe2][0x80][0x99]s divorce, the Tom Petters investigation, the Denny Hecker investigation, and many others,&#8221; Harrington said. &#8220;He claims to have been invited to speak to the Supreme Court, claims to train the &#8216;entire federal judiciary&#8217; on cybersecurity annually, and is a faculty member of the United States Judicial Conference and the Judicial College [0xe2][0x80][0x94] positions which he obtained, in part, on a house of fraudulent cards.&#8221;</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>In an interview this week, Harrington said court documents reveal that at least two of Lanterman&#8217;s previous clients complained CFS had held their data for ransom over billing disputes. In <a href="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/2022-10-26_Declaration-ofKimberlyHanlon.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">a declaration</a> (PDF) dated August "
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,132][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "2022, the co-founder of the law firm <strong>MoreLaw Minneapolis LLC</strong> said she hired Lanterman in 2014 to examine several electronic devices after learning that one of their paralegals had a criminal fraud history.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>But the law firm said when it pushed back on a consulting bill that was far higher than expected, Lanterman told them CFS would &#8220;escalate&#8221; its collection efforts if they didn&#8217;t pay, including &#8220;a claim and lien against the data which will result in a public auction of your data.&#8221;</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>&#8220;All of us were flabbergasted by Mr. Lanterman[0xe2][0x80][0x99]s email,&#8221; wrote MoreLaw co-founder <strong>Kimberly Hanlon</strong>. &#8220;I had never heard of any legitimate forensic company threatening to &#8216;auction&#8217; off an attorney[0xe2][0x80][0x99]s data, particularly knowing that the data is comprised of confidential client data, much of which is sensitive in nature.&#8221;<span id="more-70780"></span></p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>In 2009, a Wisconsin-based manufacturing company that had hired Lanterman for computer forensics balked at paying an $86,000 invoice from CFS, calling it &#8220;excessive and unsubstantiated.&#8221; The company told a Hennepin County court that on April 15, 2009, CFS conducted an auction of its trade secret information in violation of their confidentiality agreement.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>&#8220;CFS noticed and conducted a Public S"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "ale of electronic information that was entrusted to them pursuant to the terms of the engagement agreement,&#8221; the company wrote. &#8220;CFS submitted the highest bid at the Public Sale in the amount of $10,000.&#8221;</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-70891" src="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/27-cv-12-22089-ExtrusionDiesIndustries.png" alt="" width="1039" height="439" srcset="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/27-cv-12-22089-ExtrusionDiesIndustries.png 1039w, https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/27-cv-12-22089-ExtrusionDiesIndustries-768x324.png 768w, https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/27-cv-12-22089-ExtrusionDiesIndustries-782x330.png 782w" sizes="(max-width: 1039px) 100vw, 1039px" /></p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Lanterman briefly responded to a list of questions about his background (and recent heart diagnosis) on March 24, saying he would send detailed replies the following day. Those replies never materialized. Instead, Lanterman forwarded a recent memo he wrote to the court that attacked Harrington and said his accuser was only trying to take out a competitor. He has not responded to further requests for comment.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>&#8220;When I attended Upsala, I was a commuter student who lived with my grandparents in Morristown, New Jersey approxim"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "ately 30 minutes away from Upsala College,&#8221; Lanterman <a href="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/ACU-Plasmold-Lanterman-Repsonse-Letter.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">explained to the judge</a> (PDF) overseeing <a href="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/2025-03-12_memo-toCourt-1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">a separate ongoing case</a> (PDF) in which he has testified. &#8220;With limited resources, I did not participate in campus social events, nor did I attend graduation ceremonies. In 2023, I confirmed with Felician University [0xe2][0x80][0x94] which maintains Upsala College[0xe2][0x80][0x99]s records [0xe2][0x80][0x94] that they could not locate my transcripts or diploma, a situation that they indicated was possibly due to unresolved money-related issues.&#8221;</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Lanterman was ordered to appear in court on April 3 in the case defended by Perkins Coie, but he did not show up. Instead, he sent a message to the judge withdrawing from the case.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>&#8220;I am 60 years old,&#8221; Lanterman <a href="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/lanterman-retire.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">told the judge</a>. &#8220;I created my business from nothing. I am done dealing with the likes of individuals like Sean Harrington. And quite frankly, I have been planning at turning over my business to my children for years. That "
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "time has arrived.&#8221;</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Lanterman&#8217;s letter leaves the impression that it was his decision to retire. But according to <a href="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/affidavit-seanlanterman.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">an affidavit</a> (PDF) filed in a Florida case on March 28, Mark Lanterman&#8217;s son Sean said he&#8217;d made the difficult decision to ask his dad to step down given all the negative media attention.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p><strong>Mark Rasch</strong>, a former federal cybercrime prosecutor who now serves as counsel to the New York cybersecurity intelligence firm <a href="https://www.unit221b.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Unit 221B</a>, said that if an expert witness is discredited, any defendants who lost cases that were strongly influenced by that expert&#8217;s conclusions at trial could have grounds for appeal.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Rasch said law firms who propose an expert witness have a duty in good faith to vet that expert&#8217;s qualifications, knowing that those credentials will be subject to cross-examination.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>&#8220;Federal rules of civil procedure and evidence both require experts to list every case they have testified in as an expert for the past few years,&#8221; Rasch said. &#8220;Part of that due diligence is pulling up the results of those cases and seeing what the nature of their testimony has been.&"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "#8221;</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>Perhaps the most well-publicized case involving significant forensic findings from Lanterman was the 2018 conviction of <strong>Stephen Allwine</strong>, who was <a href="https://www.fox9.com/news/convicted-dark-net-killer-claims-innocence-i-couldnt-have-done-it" target="_blank" rel="noopener">found guilty of killing his wife</a> two years earlier after attempts at hiring a hitman on the dark net fell through. Allwine is serving a sentence of life in prison, and continues to maintain that he was framed, casting doubt on computer forensic evidence found on 64 electronic devices taken from his home.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "<p>On March 24, Allwine <a href="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/78.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">petitioned a Minnesota court</a> (PDF) to revisit his case, citing the accusations against Lanterman and his role as a key witness for the prosecution.</p>[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:18,133][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-24 << "]]></content:encoded>[\n]"
